N","question":"The portal of entry for the poliovirus is:"},{"id":"nmcn_023","topic":"Community Health Nursing","correct":"B","options":{"A":"Mass antibiotic administration","B":"Provision of clean water and proper sanitation","C":"Distribution of mosquito nets","D":"Mandatory hospitalization of all cases"},"examType":"NMCN-RN","question":"The most effective method of cholera prevention in a community is:"},{"id":"nmcn_058","topic":"Community Health Nursing","correct":"A","options":{"A":"Diphtheria, pertussis, tetanus, hepatitis B, and Haemophilus influenzae type B","B":"Polio, measles, rubella, mumps, and tetanus","C":"Tuberculosis, diphtheria, pertussis, tetanus, and polio","D":"Hepatitis B, measles, yellow fever, pertussis, and tetanus"},"examType":"NMCN-RN","question":"In the Expanded Programme on Immunization (EPI) in Nigeria, the pentavalent vaccine protects against:"},{"id":"nmcn_029","topic":"Community Health Nursing","correct":"C","options":{"A":"Evaluating the interventions","B":"Setting priorities","C":"Defining the community","D":"Implementing programs"},"examType":"NMCN-RN","question":"The first step in community assessment is:"},{"id":"nmcn_115","topic":"Fundamental Nursing Sciences","correct":"B","options":{"A":"Dorothea Orem","B":"Virginia Henderson","C":"Betty Neuman","D":"Hildegard Peplau"},"examType":"NMCN-RN","question":"The nursing theorist known for the ''14 Basic Human Needs'' is:"},{"id":"nmcn_089","topic":"Nursing Ethics & Professionalism","correct":"C","options":{"A":"Autonomy","B":"Beneficence","C":"Confidentiality","D":"Justice"},"examType":"NMCN-RN","question":"A nurse tells a client, ''If you don''t cooperate with treatment, I will tell your family about your HIV status.'' This is a violation of:"},{"id":"nmcn_068","topic":"General Nursing Principles","correct":"B","options":{"A":"Clamp the tube for 2 hours after each meal","B":"Measure and record the drainage output","C":"Irrigate the tube with tap water every hour","D":"Remove the tube at the end of each shift"},"examType":"NMCN-RN","question":"A nurse is caring for a client with a nasogastric tube on free drainage. The nurse should:"},{"id":"nmcn_010","topic":"General Nursing Principles","correct":"B","options":{"A":"18 gauge, 1 inch","B":"21-23 gauge, 1½ inches","C":"25 gauge, ½ inch","D":"27 gauge, 5/8 inch"},"examType":"NMCN-RN","question":"A nurse prepares to administer an intramuscular injection to an adult. The appropriate needle size is:"},{"id":"nmcn_147","topic":"Home Health Care Nursing","correct":"B","options":{"A":"Dry gauze dressing","B":"Hydrocolloid or hydrogel dressing to promote autolytic debridement","C":"Cotton wool dressing","D":"No dressing required"},"examType":"NMCN-RN","question":"A home health care nurse visits a patient with a pressure ulcer. The nurse notes the ulcer is covered with necrotic tissue. The most appropriate dressing to debride the wound is:"}]')
